gst patch for REA (rea-agents 6.9.0, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 morluto, https://github.com/morluto/rea)

feat(il2cpp): make the metadata input and complete-report allowances configurable

inspect_il2cpp_metadata refuses a linked binary_path report above the fixed
64 MiB complete-report allowance (OUTPUT_BYTES) and metadata files above the
fixed 256 MiB input allowance (INPUT_BYTES). A Unity 6000.3 game with a
160 MB GameAssembly.dll and a 32 MB global-metadata.dat (metadata v39) cannot
be linked at all under those constants.

- max_input_bytes / max_output_bytes request fields (MCP schema, CLI
  --max-input-bytes / --max-output-bytes), 1..2 GiB.
- Runtime settings il2cpp.max_input_bytes / il2cpp.max_output_bytes
  (update_analysis_settings) and launch settings REA_IL2CPP_MAX_INPUT_BYTES /
  REA_IL2CPP_MAX_OUTPUT_BYTES; request > runtime > launch > default.
- Defaults unchanged (256 MiB, 64 MiB); invalid settings are refused, never
  replaced by the default.
- Refusals name the effective allowance, its source and how to raise it; the
  1 GiB binary_path allowance stays fixed.

Apply on the tag rea-agents-6.9.0 with `git apply` (see docs/tools/rea.md).
